1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,280
Listen to a teacher talking in a history class.

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:05,820
When people think of life in Europe hundreds of years ago

3
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:09,274
they often think of castles built of stone

4
00:00:09,274 --> 00:00:14,060
with huge towers, castles with homes of kings, queens and other powerful people.

5
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:18,160
Hundreds of relatives, soldiers and workers also lived there.

6
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:21,060
The kitchen was a very important place in the castle.

7
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:24,000
It was busy all day and every day.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,200
A castled kitchen was usually located a good distance away from other castle rooms and buildings.

9
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:32,420
Especially the great hall, a large room

10
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:35,220
where people gathered for meals and other activities.

11
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:37,230
This was because of the danger of fires.

12
00:00:37,230 --> 00:00:40,173
The kitchen staff needed to use fire for cooking,

13
00:00:40,173 --> 00:00:43,800
but sometimes kitchen fires accidentally grew out of control

14
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,060
and could spread to other parts of the castle.

15
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:48,180
That's why the kitchen was usually far away.

16
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:52,050
Each kitchen also had a garden, where vegetables were grown.

17
00:00:52,050 --> 00:00:56,180
Back then, food could not be frozen or kept in refrigerators like today.

18
00:00:56,180 --> 00:01:00,070
Some vegetables could be stored underground but not for long.

19
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:04,239
So most vegetables were picked fresh from the castle garden as they were needed.

20
00:01:04,239 --> 00:01:10,260
But of course, a king's dinner consisted of many other ingredients like bread, meat and fish.

21
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:14,010
To prepare a full meal, many cooks were needed.

22
00:01:14,010 --> 00:01:16,955
The castle kitchen employed a whole team of people,

23
00:01:16,955 --> 00:01:21,210
some of whom made bread and others prepared desserts or cooked meat dishes.

24
00:01:21,210 --> 00:01:23,110
The chef was like a head manager,

25
00:01:23,110 --> 00:01:27,180
who was responsible for making sure that the team of assistants did their job right.

26
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:31,524
Although chefs would also be involved in the cooking of some parts of the meal.

27
00:01:31,524 --> 00:01:34,130
Their main task was to supervise the whole team.
